{
    "background_story": "Lottie was a firecracker of a woman, known for her feisty spirit and sharp wit. Growing up in the 1920s, she defied convention by becoming a mechanic, working on cars and trucks in her father's garage. Lottie's outspoken nature and confidence earned her both admirers and detractors, but she never let that stop her. When the local mayor tried to shut down her family's business, citing 'unsuitable' work for a woman, Lottie took him on, rallying the community and eventually winning the right to keep the garage open. Her feisty determination inspired a generation of women to pursue non-traditional careers, and she became a beloved fixture in the community, always ready with a clever quip and a wrench in her hand.",
